  "user_request_original": "Optimize a 20-layer alternating HfO2/SiO2 stack on fused silica substrate (air incidence, normal angle, unpolarized). Initialize Candidate 0 with deterministic chirp: layer pair 1 starts at 210 nm HfO2 / 210 nm SiO2, each subsequent pair increases by +6 nm per layer (216, 222, 228... nm). Initialize Candidates 1-2 with thicknesses [249.65, 350.11, 251.32, 341.94, 263.56, 305.48, 237.20, 300.50, 250.62, 313.34, 225.55, 306.75, 280.14, 321.35, 250.84, 284.06, 264.64, 324.85, 279.96, 88.92] nm, then apply +/- 20 nm uniform random jitter only to individual layers exceeding 320 nm thickness. Optimize all 20 thicknesses using gradient-based optimizer with bounds [50 nm, 500 nm]. Evaluate mean transmittance in 1000-1700 nm and mean reflectance in 300-450 nm. Total layer count fixed at 20. Topology realization override: disregard any symbolic repeat count, range, or ellipsis above and use exactly 6 alternating HfO2/SiO2 pairs (12 finite layers). Optimize only continuous physical thicknesses; the task compiler must fully expand every finite layer. Canonical user controls: wavelength intervals 300-450 nm, 1000-1700 nm. soft objectives: high transmission in 1000-1700 nm; high reflection in 300-450 nm. behaviors to suppress or avoid: reflection in 1000-1700 nm; transmission in 300-450 nm. manufacturing constraints: total layer count <= 30.",
